## Command Examples

Show every command as a single unbroken line, however long, never split across lines with trailing backslashes.

Use long-form flags everywhere, `--verbose` rather than `-v`, so a reader understands the command without consulting its help text. The exception is a tool with no long form, such as BSD xargs.

Quote a shell argument only when it needs quoting — spaces, globs, or other characters the shell would interpret. Leave plain arguments like memo.mp3 bare.

Paste real output into README examples. Run the tool, capture its stdout, and use that verbatim rather than inventing output or leaving a stale block in place.
